A||||6||horseman||Performance coil help please||||5||
Z||000000||horseman||11-11-2000||09:34 AM||||After unsuccessfully looking for a perf. coil for my 84 2.5, I opted to go with a universal. I chose the MSD SS for hei. Alright I mounted it up, but now to the wiring.I guess I need to cut the factory connector off but which wires will go where on the new coil? The coil has 2 terminals(threaded).The instructions are weak(bleak?)and I don't want to fry anything.Thanks in advance!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||11-11-2000||09:58 AM||||Red goes on the + and white goes on the -.<BR>Don't forget that the tach filter ties in there somewhere too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-11-2000||11:43 AM||||Why don't you return it and get the right coil. MSD and Accell both make coils that plug into GM factory harness connectors. Both catalogs are available online. <A HREF="http://www.msdignition.com" TARGET=_blank>www.msdignition.com</A>  and <A HREF="http://www.mrgasket.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrgasket.com</A>  respectivly. Once you have a part number you can order it anywhere that carries those lines, including the online parts shops. <P>Frankly on a 4 cyl a new ACDelco HEI coil would have been just fine. The AC coil is built to work with all external coil HEI which means it's built to handle V6 and some V8 applications. The 4 cyl reds at 4500 the V6 reds at 6000+ depending which one. You do the math but I doubt you out wind the AC coil on a 4.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||horseman||11-11-2000||07:59 PM||||To theogre: Good thought except EVERY coil that has been ordered in has the wrong connector for my vehicle. I DON'T have the GM dual connector. My coil was a 4bladed male and larger in size than the aftermarket versions inc. ACCEL(pn140011),MSD blaster,Mallory,Crane fireball(lx91) etc.<BR>I thought I made the best comprimise but am open to a solution. Thanks,<BR>Charlie||||reg||9
Z||000004||horseman||11-11-2000||08:09 PM||||I checked applications and none were avaliable for 1984 2.5 w/ext.coil. This is based upon mumerous visits to 4 different parts stores(not Auto Junk Zone). I also searched the web at Jeg's,Summit,MRGasket,Crane,Msd,Mallory etc.<BR>Not only that; try and buy a set of wires for it with the 135 boot ends. I was lucky enough to find a guy who makes universal sets of Taylor Spiro's for v-8 with the 135 ends. I bought a set for $49.95. Now I have enough for two sets of 4cyl.s.<BR>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||11-11-2000||09:24 PM||||I guess you'll have to cut it then. that or change to a later coil version and harness connector. Is this another one of those bloody 84 only things?<P>I had one of the screw terminal coils on a ford. If you are going to go that route get some crimp on eye terminals for the wire and some heatshrink.<P>work a little dielectric grease into the wire and the crimp. slide the heat shrink down the wire, crimp on the eye and then shrink the tubing over the crimp. (you want about an inch of tube.) the dielectric will seal out water and the heatshrink will help keep the wire from breaking off.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||horseman||11-11-2000||09:58 PM||||Great advice on the connections theogre but what goes where? Am I going to have to do some sort of key on-key off procedure? has anyone else encountered this with an '84 duke?<BR>Charlie||||reg||5
